{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Home for Christmas felt like a natural choice because I repeatedly chose Christmas albums, giving me a concrete reason to try it.",
    "Christmas At Downton Abbey also connected with my holiday listening, although that connection alone was not enough for me to choose it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Titles such as Heritage, Wallflower, and Annie did not establish a clear connection with the music I had chosen, so I would pass.",
    "Recognizing Nat King Cole did not make his broader collection appealing enough; my history does not establish that I want to explore his catalog."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Warm or sentimental titles such as Thinking of Home and Songs From The Heart seemed to be treated as a connection, but that mood alone does not tell me whether I will enjoy the music.",
    "A best-of collection is not automatically relevant to me; I need a connection to the artist or songs before I would choose it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My Christmas choices happened close together in late November 2014, while my latest interaction was The New Old Fashioned in September 2016; holiday listening may reflect an earlier occasion rather than my current interest.",
    "I rarely choose something without a clear reason, so a shared Christmas theme can make an album relevant without making it something I would actually try."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my past Christmas listening, but most gave me too little connection to my latest choice to motivate another interaction."
}"}
